[351.123023, "o", "\u001b[0m# \u001b[0mTodos\r\n[✓] Milestone 0: baseline mvn test (13 green), inspect smell\r\n[✓] Milestone 1: EXPAND — create ItemUpdater + 4 abstract rule classes, mvn test\r\n[✓] Milestone 2a: MIGRATE AgedBrie (move_method, rename, rewire, test)\r\n[✓] Milestone 2b: MIGRATE BackstagePass\r\n[✓] Milestone 2c: MIGRATE Sulfuras\r\n[✓] Milestone 2d: MIGRATE Regular\r\n[✓] Milestone 3: CONTRACT — chain iteration, drop dead helpers/constants, mvn test\r\n[✓] Epilogue: prove equivalence, trace one item through chain\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[359.957117, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mmvn test 2>&1 | grep -E \"Tests run:|BUILD\"\r\n[\u001b[1;34mINFO\u001b[m] \u001b[1;32mTests run: \u001b[0;1;32m12\u001b[m, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0, Time elapsed: 0.223 s -- in gildedrose.\u001b[1mGildedRoseTest\u001b[m\r\n[\u001b[1;34mINFO\u001b[m] \u001b[1;32mTests run: \u001b[0;1;32m1\u001b[m, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0, Time elapsed: 0.105 s -- in gildedrose.\u001b[1mTexttestFixtureGoldensTest\u001b[m\r\n[\u001b[1;34mINFO\u001b[m] \u001b[1;32mTests run: 13, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\u001b[m\r\n[\u001b[1;34mINFO\u001b[m] \u001b[1;32mBUILD SUCCESS\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[368.65871, "o", "All milestones complete. Final `mvn test` → **Tests run: 13, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 — BUILD SUCCESS**, golden master byte-identical.\r\n\r\n**What happened**\r\n- **M0** — baseline 13 green; smell confirmed: name-string if/else + four private helpers.\r\n- **M1 EXPAND** — added `ItemUpdater` + four abstract rule shells (`canHandle` only), legacy untouched, 13 green.\r\n- **M2 MIGRATE** — per type (`AgedBrie` → `BackstagePass` → `Sulfuras` → `Regular`): `move_method` moved the helper into its rule, `analyze_refactoring` renamed it to `update`, I finished the contract (`final` class, `public @Override`), then rewired the branch. 13 green after each.\r\n- **M3 CONTRACT** — replaced the ladder with `List<ItemUpdater>` chain iteration in `GildedRose.apply`, dropped dead helpers and the three name constants.\r\n\r\n**Trace of an Aged Brie:** `GildedRose.updateQuality` → `apply(brie)` → `AgedBrieUpdater.canHandle` returns `true` (name equals `\"Aged Brie\"`) → `AgedBrieUpdater.update` runs → `return`. A normal item misses the first three rules and falls through to `RegularUpdater`, whose `canHandle` always returns `true`.\r\n\r\nOnly direct writes were new files, the `private → public/@Override/final` contract finishing, dispatcher call-site rewires, and the final dead-code cleanup; all code movement went through `move_method`/`rename`.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
